#REQUIRES -Version 2.0
<#
=====================================================================================================================================
.SYNOPSIS
	Emails users who's passwords are due to expire within the next 3 days
.DESCRIPTION
	This script loops through all enabled AD User accounts with a valid email address.
    A CSV Report is saved to the path specified in the path parameter.
    An email is generated to the user if their password is due to expire within number of days specified in $days,
	but greater than 0 days to ensure emails do not so to accounts with expired passowrd.
	Make sure to edit and change the PARAM section to match your environment
.PARAMETER SearchBase
    Specify the full FQDN of the OU you wish to begin your search at. Default $null to search whole AD
.PARAMETER ReportPath
    Path to save the CSV file report
.PARAMETER From
	When emailing the reports, this parameter will specify who the report is 
	coming from.  
.PARAMETER To
	Tell the script where to send the email. blank by default as script will email individaul users
.PARAMETER Subject
    Subject title of the email
.PARAMETER SMTPServer
	This needs to be the IP address or name of your SMTP relay server.
.PARAMETER SMTPBODY
    The default body of text. set to Null as handled in the function
.OUTPUTS
	CSV:	ExpiringReport.csv in the $Path location
	Email:	Plan text email sent to users with expiring passwords.
    Log:    Logfile saved to Logs directory
.EXAMPLE
	.\PasswordExpiry.ps1
	Accepts all defaults as defined in the PARAM section
.EXAMPLE
	.\PasswordExpiry.ps1 -Path d:\myreports -Days 3 -From script@yourdomain.com -To Administrator@yourdomain.com -Subject "Password Expiry" -SMTPServer 192.168.1.25
	Runs the report using D:\myreports as the path to save the CSV report.  Email will be sent
	from "script@yourdomain.com" and sent to "Administrator@yourdomain.com" using 192.168.1.25
	as the SMTP relay server.  All user accounts that will be expiring in 3 days will be reported.
.NOTES
	File Name      : PasswordExpiry.ps1  
    Version        : v1.5
    Author         : Steve McIntyre
    Prerequisite   : PowerShell V2/3.
    Twitter        : @SteveMacNZ
	
Changelog
